# Build context rules for server/Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THIS FILE LIVES AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT
# ------------------------------------------
# The Docker build client looks for `.dockerignore` in the *root directory of the
# build context* -- never next to the Dockerfile. render.yaml sets
# `dockerContext: .`, so the context is the repository root, and this is the
# file that takes effect.
#
# The only thing that would override it is `server/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, the
# Dockerfile-specific naming convention, which wins over the context-root file.
# There is deliberately no such file next to server/Dockerfile, so the list
# below is the only one in play. Adding one there would silently change what
# reaches the image without changing anything in this file.
#
# WHAT IT BUYS
# ------------
# server/Dockerfile copies only server/build.gradle.kts, server/settings.gradle.kts
# and server/src. Everything matched below is dead weight in the context.
#
# Render clones the repository before building, so only git-tracked files are
# actually shipped; build outputs and local Gradle caches never reach the daemon
# in the first place, because .gitignore already covers them. The Android module
# is tracked, and it is by far the largest part of the repository, so excluding
# it is the change that actually matters.
#
# MATCHING RULES TO KEEP IN MIND
# ------------------------------
# A pattern with a single path component matches at the context root only; it
# does not match the same name nested deeper. That is why `app` excludes the
# Android module but would not have excluded a nested `app` directory. Use
# `**/` when the name should match at any depth.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT listed: `build.gradle.kts` and
# `settings.gradle.kts`. Both names also exist inside server/, and the image
# copies them. They total well under a hundred lines, so the safest thing is to
# let them travel with the context.

# --- Android application ---------------------------------------------------
app
gradlew
gradlew.bat
gradle
gradle.properties
local.properties
spotless

# --- Build output and caches ----------------------------------------------
**/build
**/.gradle
**/.kotlin
**/.cxx
**/.externalNativeBuild
captures

# --- Repository metadata and CI -------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Documentation and deployment material ---------------------------------
# Nothing under docs/ or deploy/ is copied by server/Dockerfile.
**/*.md
docs
deploy

# --- Editor, OS and agent scratch ------------------------------------------
.idea
.vs
.kilo
.opencode
.playwright-mcp
.playwright
.superpowers
.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/*.png